and we met with Jack
Black's production company.

00:27:32.840 --> 00:27:34.370
Jack Black was not there.

00:27:34.370 --> 00:27:35.910
- No, he probably never heard about it.

00:27:35.910 --> 00:27:37.420
- His development person was there

00:27:37.420 --> 00:27:39.150
and we, you know, we gave the whole pitch

00:27:39.150 --> 00:27:41.700
and we were like, all right, opening scene

00:27:41.700 --> 00:27:46.700
you got this guy who
he's in his hospital bed

00:27:47.910 --> 00:27:50.070
and then his musical therapists come in

00:27:50.070 --> 00:27:52.650
and they start playing him a song.

00:27:52.650 --> 00:27:54.980
And we actually wrote the song.

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:55.887
- 'Cause we sang the song of the pitch.

00:27:55.887 --> 00:27:58.560
- And then, 'cause we sang
the song in the pitch.

00:27:58.560 --> 00:27:59.740
Like you brought your guitar

00:27:59.740 --> 00:28:02.232
and we started singing this
song and it sounded good.

00:28:02.232 --> 00:28:04.240
- And he gets so into it

00:28:04.240 --> 00:28:06.830
that he's in the hospital
because of a heart condition

00:28:06.830 --> 00:28:08.610
and then he gets so into the performance

00:28:08.610 --> 00:28:11.250
in the opening scene that he
has a heart attack and dies.

00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:13.060
And so we get sued for malpractice,

00:28:13.060 --> 00:28:15.720
we lose our Los Angeles
practice and we have to go back

00:28:15.720 --> 00:28:18.060
